# Build configuration for a fuzzing wpa_supplicant. Copy to
# wpa_supplicant/.config:
#
#   cp defconfig-fuzz .config && make
#
# This is defconfig plus what the inverted direction needs. The hostapd one is
# hostapd/defconfig-fuzz; the two are separate builds and both are needed for
# the topology where a fuzzing station is pointed at a stock AP.
#
# Building with ASan is strongly recommended -- in the station-against-AP
# topology the *AP* is the victim, so it is the AP that wants the sanitiser,
# but a fuzzing supplicant that crashes on its own bugs is noise you want to
# see rather than guess at:
#
#   make clean
#   make CFLAGS="-fsanitize=address -fno-omit-frame-pointer -g -O1" \
#        LDFLAGS="-fsanitize=address"
#
# Checked against wpa_supplicant/defconfig at c0dca31e0.

# The fuzzing hooks themselves. Without this the mutation call sites in
# wpa_supplicant/ and src/rsn_supp/ compile away and this behaves as a normal
# station.
CONFIG_FUZZ=y

CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211=y
CONFIG_LIBNL32=y

CONFIG_IEEE80211AC=y
CONFIG_IEEE80211AX=y
CONFIG_IEEE80211BE=y

# WPA3-Personal. The station's SAE commit and confirm are two of the four
# targets this build exists to put on the air.
CONFIG_SAE=y
CONFIG_SAE_PK=y

# Mesh peering -- the third transmit direction, and the only one where both
# ends of the exchange run this same code. Off in upstream defconfig; on here,
# because without it mesh-plink and mesh-plink-ampe have no call site.
# WNM on the station side. The AP's WNM-Sleep Mode Response and its answer to
# a BSS Transition Management Query are transmit paths hostapd only takes when
# a station asks, so without this the two hooks in src/ap/wnm_ap.c are
# unreachable in every hwsim topology: the peer cannot ask.
CONFIG_WNM=y
# The station has to agree to OCV or the AP does not insert the OCI.
CONFIG_OCV=y


CONFIG_MESH=y

# AP mode, so one binary can also be the stock side of a two-node topology
# without a second build. It is NOT what gates the fuzzing hooks: the station
# and mesh hooks are outside CONFIG_AP, which is why the CONFIG_FUZZ block in
# the Makefile is outside it too.
CONFIG_AP=y

CONFIG_IEEE80211R=y

CONFIG_EAP_MD5=y
CONFIG_EAP_TLS=y
CONFIG_EAP_MSCHAPV2=y
CONFIG_EAP_PEAP=y
CONFIG_EAP_TTLS=y
CONFIG_EAP_GTC=y
CONFIG_EAP_OTP=y
CONFIG_EAP_LEAP=y
CONFIG_PKCS12=y
CONFIG_ERP=y

CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE=y
CONFIG_BACKEND=file
CONFIG_IPV6=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_FILE=y
CONFIG_INTERNAL_LIBTOMMATH=y

# hostap's own fault-injection knobs, same reasoning as the hostapd build:
# ext_mgmt_frame_handling and ext_eapol_frame_io can drive frames from outside
# without patching C.
CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS=y

# CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS' MGMT_TX control-interface command calls
# offchannel_send_action(), but nothing in the Makefile makes it pull
# offchannel.o in. Upstream's own tests/hwsim config does not hit this because
# it also sets CONFIG_P2P=y, which happens to request it. Ask for it directly
# rather than enabling a feature for its side effect -- .config is included as
# a makefile, so an internal NEED_ variable set here reaches the rule.
NEED_OFFCHANNEL=y

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream-experimental, off here as upstream has them, but each one adds a
# station transmit path the hooks above already cover -- turning any of them on
# widens what a run sends rather than only adding a feature. Expect to be the
# first to fuzz them.
#
#CONFIG_IEEE8021X_AUTH=y   # sta-auth-8021x, sta-ext-8021x-auth
#CONFIG_ENC_ASSOC=y        # sta-auth-eppke-1, sta-auth-eppke-3
#CONFIG_PQC=y
#CONFIG_FILS=y             # sta-auth-fils

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE THIS BUILD SITS RELATIVE TO UPSTREAM defconfig
#
# Every setting on which this file differs from wpa_supplicant/defconfig is
# accounted for below, and fuzzing/config/config.py --check fails both on a
# delta with no line and on a line whose delta has gone away. Turning a flag
# on to reach code is a decision about what a finding MEANS, and a run has to
# be able to say which decision it made; the ledger prints the answer beside
# the numbers. One line may cover several options where it is one decision.

# WHY CONFIG_FUZZ: the hooks. Without it the mutation call sites in
#   wpa_supplicant/ and src/rsn_supp/ compile away.
# WHY CONFIG_MESH: mesh-plink and mesh-plink-ampe have no call site without
#   it, and the mesh exchange is the only one where both ends run this same
#   code. Upstream defconfig leaves it off.
# WHY CONFIG_OCV: the station has to agree to OCV or the AP never inserts the
#   OCI, so this decides content inside frames the AP build already mutates.
# WHY CONFIG_SAE_PK: SAE-PK rides inside the SAE confirm this build already
#   sends; it widens what is in the frame rather than adding one.
# WHY CONFIG_ERP: wanted alongside the EAP methods kept below; it adds no
#   802.11 frame of its own.
# WHY CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS: ext_mgmt_frame_handling and ext_eapol_frame_io
#   drive frames from outside without patching C. Not free -- it changes real
#   behaviour on the DPP and PASN paths -- so a finding from this build
#   carries it as a condition.
# WHY NEED_OFFCHANNEL: CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS' MGMT_TX calls
#   offchannel_send_action() and nothing in the Makefile pulls offchannel.o
#   in for it. Upstream's own hwsim config does not hit this because it sets
#   CONFIG_P2P, which happens to request it; asked for directly here rather
#   than enabling a feature for its side effect.
# WHY CONFIG_INTERNAL_LIBTOMMATH: INERT, as in hostapd/defconfig-fuzz. The
#   -D sits inside `ifeq ($(CONFIG_CRYPTO), internal)` and this build does
#   not set CONFIG_CRYPTO, so it never reaches the compiler and the bignum
#   comes from OpenSSL. Set here and with no effect.

# The other direction. Upstream defconfig sets all of these and this file
# does not, so a run from this build has not covered them -- whatever its
# numbers say. The first group is the one that costs something.

# WHY CONFIG_WPS: upstream ships it on; off here. wps_parse_msg() is one of
#   the four parsers W13 instrumented and it is in NEITHER shipped binary,
#   so the wps-msg transmit target has no call site and nothing this harness
#   sends is ever read by that walker. Of all the deltas in this file this is
#   the largest single loss of parse surface.
# WHY CONFIG_P2P CONFIG_INTERWORKING CONFIG_HS20 CONFIG_MBO: upstream ships
#   all four on; off here. Together they are what makes the GAS/ANQP and P2P
#   attribute surfaces exist, and their absence is measurable rather than
#   theoretical: own-gas, own-p2p-dev and own-p2p-iface -- three of W14's six
#   source identities -- exist in no binary of this configuration.
# WHY CONFIG_DPP CONFIG_DPP2: upstream ships them on; off here, so
#   dpp_check_attrs() -- another of W13's four parsers -- is in neither
#   binary, and the dpp-tcp target has no call site.
# WHY CONFIG_TDLS: upstream ships it on; off here, so the sta-tdls transmit
#   target has no call site. One target, named, rather than a silent gap.
# WHY CONFIG_OWE: upstream ships it on; off here, so the OWE Diffie-Hellman
#   Parameter element is neither built nor parsed.

# The rest cost the sweep nothing, and are listed because the check does not
# let anything go unlisted -- which is the point: the line between "left out
# because it does not matter" and "left out because nobody noticed" is drawn
# here, by hand, rather than being left to be re-derived by whoever next
# wonders why a number looks low.

# WHY CONFIG_EAP_FAST CONFIG_EAP_GPSK CONFIG_EAP_GPSK_SHA256 CONFIG_EAP_IKEV2
#   CONFIG_EAP_PAX CONFIG_EAP_PWD CONFIG_EAP_SAKE CONFIG_EAP_TNC
#   CONFIG_SMARTCARD: EAP method bodies ride inside EAPOL-EAP frames and no
#   hook in this tree mutates one -- the EAPOL-Key hooks sit below EAP. The
#   methods kept above are what the rig's AP offers; these add nothing a
#   sweep can reach.
# WHY CONFIG_IEEE8021X_EAPOL: not set in this file and nevertheless ON in the
#   build -- the Makefile derives it from the EAP methods above. It is listed
#   because the delta is real at the level of the FILE, and it is the clearest
#   case in either config of why the ledger reports the flags the BINARY was
#   compiled with rather than the ones a .config asked for.
# WHY CONFIG_DRIVER_WEXT CONFIG_DRIVER_WIRED CONFIG_DRIVER_MACSEC_LINUX
#   CONFIG_MACSEC: the rig is hwsim, which is nl80211. The other driver
#   back ends carry no 802.11 frame construction this harness hooks.
# WHY CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE_DBUS_NEW CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE_DBUS_INTRO: the control
#   path here is the UNIX socket; D-Bus would add a build dependency and no
#   frame.
# WHY CONFIG_IBSS_RSN CONFIG_WIFI_DISPLAY CONFIG_BGSCAN_SIMPLE: features with
#   no transmit hook in this tree. IBSS RSN is the one worth revisiting if
#   the mesh work is extended, since it is the other peer-to-peer RSN.
# WHY CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG: the runs here write a file and the monitor reads
#   stdout; syslog would split the log in two.
